# Scripts and build inputs that make the packages CI publishes, and the files those scripts import or call. A
# change to any of them also needs a clean Codex security review (PROC-0001, "Review policy, 2026-11-01").
# review-gate reads this file from main, or from a PR's base branch when a ruleset requires pull requests there.
# One path per line; a path ending in / covers a folder.
#
# Only packages.yml's publish job holds the write token (packages: write), and it builds nothing: it pushes the
# bytes pack-consume made and proved. Those bytes ship as they are, so what makes them is still risky even though
# that job runs read-only. Product code and dependencies are not listed; they no longer run with the token.
#
# Keep it current: a PR that adds a script to the packing or publishing jobs adds it here.
# review-gate.sh itself counts Directory.Build.props, Directory.Build.targets and Directory.Packages.props at any
# depth. This file is under .github/, so changing it is itself risky.

# packages.yml's pack-consume runs eng/verify-packages.sh, which runs eng/verify-boundaries.sh and eng/verify.sh,
# and publish runs eng/package-proof.py. Those reach most of eng/ (scripts, tests, pins and baselines), so the whole
# folder counts.
eng/
tooling/harborline-contract-codegen/
# The publish job reads its publication authority from here.
repository.yaml
# Build-wide inputs: the feeds restore pulls from and the pinned SDK.
nuget.config
global.json
# MSBuild tasks and analyzers that the build-wide files load into every build.
tooling/Harborline.Tooling.LocalizationXliff/
packages/analyzers/
